  "tagline": "The in-memory data structure server that became the default cache, now with search, JSON and vectors built in.",
  "description": "Redis is a single-threaded-core, in-memory server for strings, hashes, lists, sets, sorted sets, streams and more, accessed over the simple RESP protocol. Since Redis 8 the former Stack modules (Query Engine with vector search, JSON, time series, probabilistic structures) ship in the core, so one binary covers caching, session storage, rate limiting, queues and semantic caching for LLM apps. Licensing is the big caveat: 7.4 moved to RSALv2/SSPLv1, and Redis 8 added AGPLv3 as a third option, which is why many clouds and distros now standardise on the BSD-licensed Valkey fork instead.",
